    {
      "id": 152477,
      "name": "Killswitch",
      "username": "Killswitch",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-01-05T19:59:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In analogy to cookware, is \"geekware\" a set of implements, containers, and devices that enables one to geek? I like it. I'll have to try a recipe out of my geekbook and invite friends and family to share my geeking.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Omnitron XVI: The latest in geekware components and devices.</p>\n<p>The sentient AI learned quickly that in order to best the resilient heroes, it must overtake the fanbase with all sorts of enticing merchandise, and spreading this vast following to the ends of the earth, until all are forced to engage in an all-out war over fandoms and all things geekery*, transforming the masses into mindless zombies craving more.</p>\n<p>*Geekery may or may not include Sentinels the lunchbox, Sentinels the breakfast cereal, Sentinels the movie, and Sentinels the flame-thrower.</p>",
      "post_number": 15,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:31:39.338Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
